.docname {Docker Compose}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Compose file | A YAML list of containers, their images, ports and volumes | `backend/telemetry/docker-compose.yml` |
    | Fragment | One service's own compose file | `backend/chat/docker-compose.yml` |
    | Dev override | A second file that changes a fragment for live editing | `docker-compose.dev.yml` |
    | `include:` | A Compose key that loads other compose files, each from its own folder | `compose.runtime.yml` |
    | Project | The group of containers Compose starts together, under one name | `crowdvision-integration-tests` |
    | Volume | Storage that outlives the container | `telemetry-data` |
    | Watch | Compose copies changed files into a running container, or rebuilds it | `develop.watch` |
    | Edge | The one entry point every browser request goes through | Caddy on port 80 |
    | `forward_auth` | Caddy asks another service "may this request pass?" before sending it on | `claims-gateway /verify` |

Locally the whole platform runs under Docker Compose. No single file lists every service: each service keeps its own compose file beside its code, and a small script joins them into one on every start.

---

## The files

| File | Holds | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `docker-compose.yml` (root) | Shared parts only: `gateway` (Caddy), `redis`, `kafka`, `keycloak`, `keycloak-db`, `prometheus`, `grafana`; includes `docker/rust-base` | — |
| `backend/<svc>/docker-compose.yml` | The service and its own database | `telemetry`, `telemetry-db` |
| `backend/<svc>/docker-compose.dev.yml` | Changes for `just stack dev`: `target: dev`, watch rules, published database ports, database browsers | `telemetry-db-gui` |
| `backend/<svc>/docker-compose.test.yml` | A throwaway stack for that service's integration tests | `telemetry-test` |
| `backend/acceptance/docker-compose.*.yml` | The cross-service acceptance stack | `integration-tests` |
| `docker/rust-base/docker-compose.yml` | The Rust build image, `scale: 0` | `rust-base` |
| `simulators/*/`, `devices/ap-collector/`, `frontend/` | Same base + dev pair | `client` |

- **Why per service.** A service is added or removed without touching a central file, and its compose file moves with it.
- **No custom networks.** No file declares `networks:`, so every container of a project joins Compose's default network and reaches the others by service name: `telemetry:3000`, `redis:6379`.
- **`backend/agent` holds 9 services**: `agent`, `agent-db`, `agent-ingester` and the Langfuse stack (`langfuse-web`, `langfuse-worker`, `langfuse-db`, `redis-langfuse`, `clickhouse`, `minio`).

---

## `just stack dev`, step by step

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant U as Developer
        participant J as just
        participant E as "scripts/env, one script per area"
        participant P as compose-run.py
        participant D as docker compose
        U->>J: just stack dev --no-agent
        J->>E: env recipe, 11 scripts in order
        E->>E: append missing secrets to the env file, rewrite RUST_VERSION
        J->>P: python3 scripts/compose/compose-run.py dev --no-agent
        P->>P: argparse, expand --no-agent to pattern agent
        P->>P: add docker-compose.yml
        P->>P: walk backend/, simulators/, devices/, skip excluded folders
        P->>P: add frontend
        P->>P: write compose.runtime.yml
        P->>D: config --format json
        P->>P: find stopped containers with a fixed name, docker rm -f them
        P->>D: config --services, drop names matching agent
        P->>D: up --watch --remove-orphans, with the kept service names
        D->>D: build images, start containers in depends_on order, watch files

| Step | What happens | Real value |
|---|---|---|
| 2 | `create`, `vapid`, `token`, `config`, `langfuse`, `keycloak`, `controlplane`, `gateway-key`, `ingest-key`, `telemetry-db`, `rust` | Each one skips a key already in `.env` |
| 3 | Only `rust.sh` rewrites a value every time | `RUST_VERSION=` the pin in `.mise.toml` |
| 5 | `--no-agent` becomes the substring `agent` | `EXCLUDE_GROUPS["agent"] = ("agent",)` |
| 7 | Each folder adds `docker-compose.yml`, and in `dev` also `docker-compose.dev.yml` | `backend/agent` skipped: printed `excluded: backend/agent` |
| 9 | One `include:` entry per folder; a pair becomes one entry with two paths | 16 entries: root, 10 backend, 3 simulators, `ap-collector`, `frontend` |
| 11 | A stopped container with a `container_name` would block `up` with a name clash | `crowd-vision-socket` |
| 12 | The root file is always included, so its services can only be dropped by name | — |
| 13 | `COMPOSE_BAKE=true`: builds go through BuildKit Bake, in parallel | — |

The generated file looks like this:

```yaml
# Auto-generated by scripts/compose/compose-run.py — do not commit.
include:
  - path: docker-compose.yml
  - path:
      - backend/chat/docker-compose.yml
      - backend/chat/docker-compose.dev.yml
  - path:
      - backend/claims-gateway/docker-compose.yml
      - backend/claims-gateway/docker-compose.dev.yml
```

`compose.runtime.yml` is in `.gitignore`.

### Why `include:` and not several `-f` flags

With `-f a.yml -f b.yml`, Compose resolves every relative path against the **first** file's folder. `build.context: ../..` in `backend/telemetry/docker-compose.yml` would then point two levels above the repo root. `include:` resolves each file against its own folder.

A pair of files is one entry because two separate entries may not define the same service: Compose stops with a conflict.

### Leaving parts out

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        A["argument"] --> F{"--no-group flag?"}
        F -- yes --> G["its patterns from EXCLUDE_GROUPS"]
        F -- no --> S["the argument itself, as a substring"]
        G --> M{"mode is down or build?"}
        S --> M
        M -- yes --> N["ignored: everything is included"]
        M -- no --> C["folder name contains it: whole fragment left out"]
        C --> V["service name contains it: left out of the up list"]

| Flag | Patterns | Leaves out |
|---|---|---|
| `--no-agent` | `agent` | `backend/agent`, all 9 services |
| `--no-metrics` | `prometheus`, `grafana` | Two root services, by name |
| `--no-simulators` | `simulator` | The three simulator folders |
| `--no-devices` | `ap-collector` | `devices/ap-collector` |
| bare word | itself | Anything whose folder or service name contains it |

**Example.** `just stack dev chat`:

1. Folder `backend/chat` contains `chat`: its two files are not included.
2. No other service name contains `chat`, so nothing else goes.

**Example of a trap.** `just stack dev db` drops every service with `db` in its name: `twin-db`, `telemetry-db`, `keycloak-db`… and the stack cannot start.

### Modes

| Recipe | Mode | Command |
|---|---|---|
| `just stack dev` | `dev` | `up --watch --remove-orphans` |
| `just stack dev --build` | `dev` | the same, plus `--build` |
| `just stack start` | `start` | `up --build -d --remove-orphans`, production stages, in the background |
| `just stack down` | `down` | `down --remove-orphans`, always everything |
| `just stack logs <svc>` | — | `docker compose -f compose.runtime.yml logs -f <svc>` |
| `--dry-run` | any | Prints the `docker` command and stops after writing the file |

---

## The edge: Caddy

`gateway` runs `caddy:2.11.7` on `${BACKEND_PORT}` (80), with the repo-root `Caddyfile` mounted read-only.

| Path | Goes to | Gated | Prefix removed |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/gateway/*` | `claims-gateway:3000` | no | yes |
| `/tenancy/*`, `/twin/*`, `/notification/*`, `/chat/*`, `/dashboard`, `/dashboard/*`, `/telemetry/*` | the service | yes | yes |
| `/socket.io/*` | `socket:3000` | yes | no: Socket.IO expects its own path |
| `/agent/*` | `agent:3000` | no, and `X-Gateway-Claims` is removed | yes |
| `/telemetry/ingest`, `/telemetry/collector`, `/telemetry/observations` | `telemetry:3000` | no: the body is HMAC-signed and checked inside `telemetry` | `/telemetry` only |
| `/prometheus/*`, `/grafana/*` | the tool | no | `/prometheus` only |
| `/<x>-db-gui/*` | the database browser of each Mongo service and `telemetry` | no | no |
| `/langfuse*` | redirect to port 3030 | — | — |

`/chat/*` adds `flush_interval -1`: answers stream as SSE, and buffering would deliver every token at the end.

### A gated request

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant B as Browser
        participant C as Caddy
        participant G as claims-gateway
        participant T as digital-twin
        B->>C: GET /twin/buildings, cookie authentication_token
        C->>G: GET /verify, same headers
        G->>G: RequireAuthentication: extractToken
        G->>G: jwt.ParseWithClaims, RS256, issuer cv-gateway
        alt token missing or bad
            G-->>C: 401
            C-->>B: 401, the service is never called
        else valid
            G->>G: verifyHandler: json.Marshal(claims), base64
            G-->>C: 200, X-Gateway-Claims
            C->>C: copy_headers X-Gateway-Claims, strip /twin
            C->>T: GET /buildings, x-gateway-claims
            T->>T: decode the header, run Cedar
            T-->>B: 200
        end

| Step | Data |
|---|---|
| 1 | `Cookie: authentication_token=eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIs…` |
| 3 | `extractToken` reads `Authorization: Bearer …` first, then the cookie |
| 4 | Signature checked against `claims-gateway`'s own public key; only `RS256` accepted |
| 8 | `{"sub":"ada","memberships":[…],"exp":…}` as standard base64 |
| 10 | Path `/twin/buildings` becomes `/buildings` |

Why the edge checks once: the services behind it never verify a signature; they read the header. The cluster does the same with Istio, so a service runs unchanged in both places: [Kubernetes & Istio](kubernetes.qd).

`gateway` lists five services in `depends_on` with `required: false`: it starts even when they are left out, and finds them when they appear, because Caddy looks up each name per request.

---

## `.env`: what `just stack env` writes

Every `dev` and `start` runs `env` first. Each script appends only what is missing, so a second run changes nothing except `RUST_VERSION`.

| Script | Writes |
|---|---|
| `create.sh` | An empty `.env`, mode 600 |
| `vapid.sh` | `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`, `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`, `VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`, a P-256 key pair; checks the lengths 87 and 43 |
| `token.sh` | `EVAL_JWT_SECRET`, 32 random bytes, local evals only |
| `config.sh` | `BACKEND_PORT=80`, `FRONTEND_PORT=8080`, `DEV_URL=http://localhost`; asks for `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` |
| `langfuse.sh` | Langfuse keys, salt, passwords |
| `keycloak.sh` | `KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD`, empty Google client fields |
| `controlplane.sh` | `INTERNAL_SIGNING_SECRET`, `TENANCY_DB_PASSWORD`, `REGISTRY_DB_PASSWORD` |
| `gateway-key.sh` | `secrets/gateway-dev-key.pem`, a 2048-bit RSA key, only if missing |
| `ingest-key.sh` | `TELEMETRY_INGEST_SECRET`, `TELEMETRY_DEVICE_MASTER_KEY` |
| `telemetry-db.sh` | `TELEMETRY_DB_PASSWORD` |
| `rust.sh` | `RUST_VERSION`, rewritten every run so a bump in `.mise.toml` reaches the build |

The RSA key is kept on disk, not regenerated: a new key would make every signed-in cookie invalid.

---

## Live reload

| Language | Watch rule | On a source change | On a dependency change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rust | `sync ./src` | `cargo watch -x run` rebuilds the service crate only | `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`: `rebuild` the image |
| Go | `sync ./` | `air` rebuilds and restarts | `go.mod`: `rebuild` |
| `agent` | `sync ./app` | `uvicorn --reload` | `pyproject.toml`: `rebuild` |
| `frontend` | `sync ./src` | Vite dev server, `npm run dev` | `package.json`: `rebuild` |

- **Rust has no `target/` volume.** The `dev` image already holds a fresh build; a volume over `target/` would hide it, and every dependency change would compile twice.
- **Go shares two volumes** across the four services: `go-mod-cache` (`/go/pkg/mod`) and `go-build-cache` (`/root/.cache/go-build`). Go locks inside the cache folders, so four containers can use them at once.
- **Mongo** runs with `--wiredTigerCacheSizeGB 0.25`. Without it each of the four instances may grow towards half the host's memory.

### Published host ports

Only the dev overrides publish database ports. Two services on one host port stop the whole `up`.

| Port | Service |
|---|---|
| 80 | `gateway` |
| 8080 | `client` (frontend) |
| 5432, 5433, 5434, 5435 | `telemetry-db`, `tenancy-db`, `registry-db`, `agent-db` |
| 27017, 27019, 27020, 27021 | `twin-db`, `notification-db`, `dashboard-db`, `chat-db` |
| 6379, 9092, 8090 | `redis`, `kafka`, `keycloak` |
| 3001, 3002, 3003 | `sensor-simulator`, `aq-simulator`, `ap-simulator` |
| 3030 | `langfuse-web` |

