## Test stacks

### One service: `just test <svc>-integration`

.mermaid
    sequenceDiagram
        autonumber
        participant J as just
        participant S as test-integration.sh
        participant D as docker compose
        participant T as telemetry-test
        J->>S: bash backend/telemetry/test-integration.sh
        S->>S: RUST_VERSION from the mise pin
        S->>S: trap down --volumes on EXIT
        S->>D: -p telemetry-integration-tests up --build --exit-code-from telemetry-test
        D->>D: start telemetry-db, telemetry-redis, telemetry-kafka
        D->>T: target dev, run scripts/test/rust-integration-tests.sh
        T-->>D: exit code
        D-->>S: same exit code
        S->>D: down --remove-orphans --volumes

| Service | Project | Infra |
|---|---|---|
| `chat` | `chat-integration-tests` | MongoDB |
| `digital-twin` | `digital-twin-integration-tests` | MongoDB |
| `notification` | `notification-integration-tests` | MongoDB, Redis, Kafka |
| `socket` | `socket-integration-tests` | Redis |
| `telemetry` | `telemetry-integration-tests` | TimescaleDB, Redis, Kafka |
| `dashboard` | `dashboard-integration-tests` | MongoDB, Redis |

- Own project name: it never touches a running `just stack dev`.
- `trap … EXIT`: under `set -e`, a failed `up` would exit before a trailing `down`.
- The tests talk to containers by name, never through a host port.

### Acceptance: `just test integration`

`backend/acceptance/run-integration-tests.sh` writes `compose.integration-tests.runtime.yml`:

| Included file | Gives |
|---|---|
| `docker/rust-base/docker-compose.yml` | The Rust build image |
| `backend/acceptance/docker-compose.infra.yml` | `redis`, `kafka` |
| `backend/{telemetry,socket,dashboard}/docker-compose.yml` | The three real services |
| `backend/acceptance/docker-compose.integration.yml` | Stubs for `digital-twin` and `claims-gateway` (nginx), the real Caddy `gateway`, and the `integration-tests` runner |

- The real `Caddyfile` is mounted, so `backend/acceptance/edge/` tests the edge that ships.
- Stub `claims-gateway` answers `/verify` with a fixed `401` and a marker, so a test can tell an edge refusal from a service one.
- It generates the telemetry keys itself, so it runs without `just stack env`.

---

## Traps

- **`just stack dev` does not rebuild by default.** Only `--build`, or a watched `rebuild` file, rebuilds an image. A `Dockerfile` change needs `--build`.
- **`--no-simulators` leaves `telemetry`'s `SIMULATORS` list as is.** Starting a simulation then fails to reach them.
- **A root service cannot leave by folder.** `prometheus`, `grafana`, `keycloak` go only by name, which is why `--no-metrics` exists.
- **`container_name` is global.** `crowd-vision-socket` is shared by the dev stack and the acceptance stack; the acceptance script removes a stopped one, never a running one.
- **Renaming a volume empties the service.** Compose names the real volume after project and key: see [Naming Conventions](naming-conventions.qd).

Related: [Docker Images](docker.qd), [Kubernetes & Istio](kubernetes.qd), [just](just.qd).
